ere, and 59% reach +6 by move 19.","Watch your knight: it is behind 25% of your lost leads, 1.4\u00d7 the usual rate, most often the king's knight (55%), landing on d4, g5, c3.","Aim at their rook: it is behind 20% of their lost leads, 1.2\u00d7 the usual rate, most often the queen's rook (64%). The reply wins it outright 32% of the time. Take it with a pawn.","Material changes hands for you on g4 and e6: build pressure there.","They win material on d4 and c4: keep those squares defended.","Look for the back-rank mate: it appears 3.5\u00d7 as often as usual in this opening."],"similar":[],"family":"Scandinavian Defense"}